  "name": "Overwhelm",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/fire/explosion-fireball-large-orange.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>Your magic does not target so much as occupy. It fills the room, folds around the people you would rather it spared, and leaves everyone else with the discovery that there was nowhere in the room that would have helped.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>When you Cast a Spell with an area, you may exclude a number of creatures from that area equal to your spellcasting attribute modifier.</li><li>You may convert a burst into a cone or line of equivalent size, or the reverse.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Once per round, when you Cast a Spell with an area, creatures in that area treat their degree of success as one lower, to a minimum of a failure.<ul><li>Creatures that critically succeed or critically fail are unaffected.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><strong>10th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Double the size of your spell areas.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>The effect from 5th level now also applies to creatures that critically succeed, reducing their result to a success.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> from 5th, switch <em>Overwhelm</em> on in your effects panel before casting the round's area spell. While it is on, every creature saving against an area spell of yours has a success treated as a failure, and from 15th a critical success as a success. Switch it off after.</p>\n<p>For the table: excluding creatures, reshaping and doubling areas. Place the template by hand; a note on every area spell lists what this talent lets you do with it.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
